{"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/ivortuning\/welltemperament\/kirnbergerii"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"patch":0,"major":0},"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"text":"static","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"var","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"kirnbergerII","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:10IvorTuning15WellTemperamentV","text":"WellTemperament","kind":"typeIdentifier","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorTuning\/documentation\/IvorTuning\/WellTemperament"},{"text":" { ","kind":"text"},{"text":"get","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" }","kind":"text"}],"platforms":["macOS"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"content":[{"text":"Discussion","anchor":"discussion","level":2,"type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Two fifths — D→A and A→E — are each narrowed by ½ of the syntonic comma, equal to"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"√(20\/9) ≈ 691.202 cents. One fifth — F♯→C♯ — is narrowed by one schisma"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"(32805:32768), equal to 16384:10935 ≈ 699.977 cents. The remaining nine fifths are"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"pure (3:2). The circle closes exactly because one syntonic comma times one schisma"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"equals one Pythagorean comma."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The two half-comma fifths are unusually flat, giving C-adjacent keys very pure"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"thirds while keys with many sharps or flats suffer greatly."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"kind":"content"}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/IvorTuning\/documentation\/IvorTuning","doc:\/\/IvorTuning\/documentation\/IvorTuning\/WellTemperament"]]},"kind":"symbol","sections":[],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/IvorTuning\/documentation\/